Version 0.4.3
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-16

Highlights

- A refreshed Cassini, with paper and graphite surfaces, navy accents, clearer
  status badges and six distinct speaker colours. The first window introduces
  recording with a new welcome screen, and the browser companion shares the look.
- Read long meetings smoothly. Transcripts scroll without jumping, show short
  interjections inline, and keep word playback, search and keyboard navigation
  connected to the right speaker.
- Bring more recordings into your Library. Import MP3, M4A, WAV and FLAC audio,
  several meeting files at once, or a ZIP archive. Export selected meetings or
  your Library as a ZIP, and written-down meetings as text or SRT/WebVTT subtitles
  under More formats.
- Find and organise meetings more easily. Search matches meeting titles as well
  as spoken words, including recordings not yet written down. Star meetings,
  switch between All and Starred, and narrow search results with shared filters.
- Set up Saved voices with one question, or add your voice by reading a short
  phrase aloud. Rename or delete saved voices, and use the revised Name a speaker
  dialog while listening. Voiceprints stay on this computer.

Before you update

- After upgrading, log out and back in so the new version takes effect.
- The bundled browser companion is now version 0.2.31. Follow the companion
  setup instructions to refresh an older browser installation.
- Once downloaded, the more accurate Parakeet Ultra model is used automatically.
  Whistle remains built in. The Parakeet Ultra download suggestion now appears
  in the Library sidebar, with model downloads managed in Preferences.

Improvements

- Recording and meeting details sit alongside the Library. Recording controls,
  audio-source details and saving feedback are clearer, and stopping a recording
  shows its saving state immediately.
- See the steps and progress while a meeting is being written down. Stop and
  keep the progress, then resume later; queued work resumes after recording ends.
- Browser recordings can capture your voice directly from the call’s microphone
  stream without opening another microphone. Automatic recording requires fresh,
  verified call evidence and respects Stop and Stop All.
- Browse Trash inside Cassini, restore a meeting or delete it permanently. Help
  is available from the app menu, including offline, and Keyboard shortcuts lists
  the current controls.
- Imported recordings show progress and useful failure messages. Unsupported
  files are reported as ignored; damaged files and a full disk have clear
  explanations, with Try again when freeing space can resolve the problem.
- Meeting rows, playback controls, speaker naming and search share a more
  consistent layout, including narrow windows and translated status labels.

Fixes

- Imported and exported meetings keep their original recording date across
  time zones.
- Imported 16 kHz Opus voice notes can now be written down successfully.
- Other people in browser recordings can be separated into speakers. Browser
  reconnects and recording completion handle queued work more reliably.
- Recording keeps audio-source updates and the explanation when browser sound
  switches to computer audio. Stop remains effective during pending operations.
- Naming a speaker no longer returns focus to an outdated listening selection.
  Transcript colours, speaker attribution and playback links stay consistent
  across the meeting view, search and the standalone reader.

Version 0.4.2
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-08

After upgrading, log out and back in so the new version takes effect.

- Listen by speaker. After a meeting is written down, play one person’s turns
  in order, move between turns or speakers, replay a turn, and name or merge
  speakers while listening. A listening bar shows who is speaking, where you
  are, and an excerpt. It also works in narrow windows.
- Follow the recording more easily. The transcript highlights the current
  turn. Select a time to play from there or a name to listen to that person.
  Speaker markers and a hover readout help you find your place on the
  timeline. Keyboard navigation and Shift+Enter work with the transcript; the
  playback skip is ten seconds.
- Nextcloud Talk discovery is fixed. Calls that previously failed to appear in
  Cassini can now be discovered. The bundled browser companion is version
  0.2.25, with better recovery through reloads and temporary connection loss.
- Clearer companion setup and health. Cassini explains when companion files
  are missing or out of date, and when a particular browser tab needs
  reloading. Idle browsers no longer cause misleading warnings. Recording
  details retain the reason browser sound stopped, even after the recording is
  saved and reopened.
- Participant names stay with the audio. Names supplied by the meeting page
  are preserved with the recorded audio sources, including through retries,
  and appear in Recording details.
- An alert when recording switches to computer audio. If an automatic
  recording loses browser sound and switches to the computer’s audio, Cassini
  alerts you once and keeps the explanation visible. The alert also works when
  the Recording page is already open and after a temporary companion
  reconnect.
- More reliable recording and clearer missing-audio reports. Stopping or
  changing sources preserves queued sound and records any known audio loss
  accurately. Browser reconnection timing is more reliable, and a rare crash
  while checking muted computer audio is fixed.
- A cleaner panel indicator. Fixes duplicate recording timers caused by
  AppIndicator discovery and relaunching Cassini.
- Better background-service recovery and logs. Cassini detects an old browser
  connection service after an upgrade and refreshes it when it is idle.
  Startup failures and connection problems now leave local diagnostic logs
  that remain available after the window closes.
- Clean upgrades from cassini-viewer. The Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora, openSUSE and
  Arch packages replace older cassini-viewer packages properly. Your Library
  stays where it is.
- Preparation for future call signals. Cassini can now use verified call-
  status information from the companion to manage automatic computer-audio
  recordings under your existing preference. No site provides verified call
  detection through this feature yet; WhatsApp remains unverified. Playing
  music, a video or a voice message alone does not automatically start a
  recording.

Version 0.4.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-06

After upgrading, log out and back in so the new version takes effect.

- Speaker names wrap correctly, including in wide windows.
- Play buttons in Search stay usable with a screen reader when results refresh.
- Stopping a browser recording stays stopped until you choose to record again
  or turn automatic recording back on. Starting the next recording works
  reliably while the previous one finishes saving.
- Browser recordings keep up to ten seconds of incoming sound while the
  computer is busy, and Stop stays responsive during saving.
- The browser companion is now version 0.2.15, with more accurate timing
  through brief browser stalls.

Version 0.4.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-11-05

Cassini is now called Cassini talk. Your Library stays in Music/Cassini.

- Recording starts reliably when the computer is silent: the other people's
  side waits for the first sound instead of failing the start
- When a microphone or the computer's sound cannot open, Cassini says why and
  keeps recording what did open; if nothing opened, no empty meeting is left
  behind. Quit no longer waits for a microphone that never delivers audio
- Silent sources are saved as exact silence, so writing down and speaker
  separation skip them instead of reading noise
- Every part of Cassini places each track at the same start, so playback,
  transcripts and speakers line up; words stay inside the time a person was
  present, and a turn never spans a gap. Cassini for Mac passes the same check
- Browser meetings: set up the companion from Cassini, connect in the
  background, keep recording through page reloads, record automatically only
  once a call has really started, and record with no window open. Browser and
  computer audio share one clock, even when the system clock is adjusted
  during a meeting. The companion is now version 0.2.13: a long silent stretch
  no longer slows a browser recording's clock
- GNOME and Mac pass the same end-to-end tests: a recording followed live
  while it is in progress (shared test 2), and the same three outcome files
  (shared test 8)
- While recording: a live spectrogram for each side, Recording details that
  show what is being captured, a warning when muted output would silence the
  computer's sound, and a test recording to check your setup
- Library: move meetings to Trash with five seconds to undo, rename with F2,
  and keep each saved meeting as a portable Cassini file
- Writing down shows its progress before the first words, reads a track again
  without voice detection when it finds too few words there, and names the app
  version when it downloads models
- Translated into Italian, French, Spanish and Portuguese (Brazil and Portugal)
- Many capture fixes: interrupted and re-anchored inputs, frozen browser
  connections, and a live spectrum that no longer stops after the window
  stalls

Version 0.3.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-29

- Reconnect the browser companion with Connect in Cassini after updating.
  Native host identifiers now use io.codemyriad; do not rerun install-host.py
  with an old extension ID
- Keep recordings and received meetings in the Library, play their transcripts,
  search across meetings, and import or export audio and transcripts
- Record browser meetings independently, with a microphone choice for each one;
  optionally record meetings automatically while the window is closed
- Choose What is recorded during a meeting; keep recording this computer's sound
  if the browser connection is lost
- Set up the browser companion from Cassini, including in the Flatpak
- Write meetings down locally with bundled Whistle, or download the optional
  Parakeet Ultra model; the packages include both engines on x86_64
- Tell speakers apart with an optional model, name or clear their names, merge
  speakers and undo merges
- Remember saved voices locally, recognise them in new meetings, play samples,
  and forget individual voices or everyone
- Keep audio aligned when an input is interrupted, without adding silence for
  gradual device-clock drift

Version 0.2.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-27

- Record meetings: microphone and desktop audio into an Opus file
- Record browser meetings source by source with the companion extension for
  Chromium-based browsers; its native messaging hosts are registered per user
- Optionally record every browser meeting automatically, with a Stop notification
- Name missing libraries and GStreamer plugins at startup
- Packages for Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora, openSUSE, Arch Linux and Alpine, built and
  tested with the same scripts locally and in CI

Version 0.1.1
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

- Fix transcript-click crashes and GTK label sizing warnings
- Keep participants visible and rejoin interrupted speech with inline interjections
- Preserve interjections in exports

Version 0.1.0
~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Released: 2026-10-15

First release.

- Play Cassini portable meetings with a transcript that follows playback
- Click words and timestamps to seek
- Speaker filter, transcript chooser, search
- Summary view with action items and topics
- Audio integrity check (exact-opus-audio-v1)
- Export as text or WebVTT
